<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlos, Duke of Madrid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1909">1909</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Carlos VII (Carlist pretender)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlos, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, was the Carlist claimant to the Spanish throne as Carlos VII from 1868. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-carlist-war">Third Carlist War</a> of 1872–1876, setting up a court and administration at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estella-lizarra">Estella</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> that governed much of the Basque Country and Navarre. After his defeat he went into exile, and he later also claimed the French throne as Legitimist heir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlos-duke-of-madrid.jpg" alt="Carlos, Duke of Madrid" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D._Carlos_de_Borb%C3%B3n_y_de_Austria-Este_smoking.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
